{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1030200-telekinetically-controlled-weapons","id":1030200,"title":"Telekinetically Controlled Weapons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-11T12:59:37-08:00","id":1030200,"title":"Telekinetically Controlled Weapons","content":"Obviously the base use of telekinetic, concussive power is a straight Forces attack. Iterator Tony Stark uses his gauntlets to strike his foes with a repulser blast.<br /> <br /> But how do you handle telekinetically controlling an object and using it to attack foes? The two most common uses is 1) lift an object (rock, chair, etc) and chuck it at someone, and 2) making a weapon float around for an extended period and use it to make melee attacks (the classic floating sword trick). I don't know if the Mage books ever went into how to mechanically adjudicate that sort of combat, so I wanted everyone's input.<br /> <br /> In the first case, it's an aimed attack, done as a &quot;no-hands&quot; throw in the same way you'd attack with a thrown weapon (Dexterity + Athletics). But obviously you aren't using your Dexterity - no hands - and it's questionable whether you'd use Athletics. In the second case, you'd normally use Dexterity + Melee to wield a sword, but this time without touching the weapon. Again, you wouldn't be using your Dexterity.<br /> <br /> So what do you use? What other Attribute (and Abilities perhaps) would stand in for the normal ones, if you're aiming without your body? I would think either Manipulation or Wits for the Attribute. One could argue that Athletics and Melee don't just apply to the physical element of their use, but also the understanding of theory and application. As such, one's Ability knowledge in this area might transfer over, since a person trying to send a rock flying needs to know how objects move given a certain level of force, and a person trying to wield a floating blade still needs to understand openings, leverage, and edge alignment. A technomancer might see throwing an object with their gravity gun to be a physics problem more than an athletic one, and might logically substitute Science.<br /> <br /> Then there's the matter of damage. A thrown object would obviously have as much damage behind it as was generated on the Arete roll. But a melee weapon that's being controlled for an extended period would benefit more from Duration than Damage. Would one need to generate successes for both? Or would you use some other stat to determine a floating sword's base damage (and if so, which one)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:05:45-08:00","id":1030204,"title":"","content":"Just treat it like Psychokinesis in Sorcerer: Revised, which is to replace Dexterity with Wits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T14:57:49-08:00","id":1030265,"title":"","content":"I'd treat it akin to 'better body' Only rather than upgrading your body to perform well, you're obviating it's use in favor of something else. So, for every success, you get 1-2 points (I don't recall at the moment.) in a stat, Either Dexterity or Strength for your telekinetic force. And obviously you'd have to use correspondence, depending on how far away this telekinesis is.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you'd need to roll duration to keep it floating for a long while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}